Having accomplished my first four ascensions in the last year, I had
begun to think of myself as a Nethack player of some modest level of
skill.  But yesterday, I died in three consecutive games, none lasting
more than an hour.

First game, on the first level of Sokoban, as I was trudging back to
start rolling the next-to-last boulder, the game spawned a leocrotta
in the level's large room, just before I came around the corner.
Me:   "U, U, U.  Wait, what's this about a leocrotta?  Oh, I'm dead
already?  CRAP."

Next game, a bunch of elves snuck into the dark room I was exploring,
and surrounded me as I skipped merrily towards an exit.  Elbereth was
of course of no avail.  After they spanked me down to 1 HP, I
consulted my inventory.  My best chance seemed to be reading one of my
unidentified scrolls, two cursed, one uncursed.  I read the uncursed
one, which turned out to be ID.  I got four IDs out of it--how lucky!--
but then quickly died on the next turn.

Next game, I simply thought my prayer timeout had expired when it
hadn't, and got slaughtered while praying.

One of those games was especially heartbreaking, since I had found a
HUGE rare books shop, gathered up the entire inventory, and IDed the
lot with a single blessed ID scroll.  Then I teleported out and (IIRC)
rose from level 3 to 6 just by dispatching the Kops that came after
me.

These three games came on the heels of another in which I'd been
sacfesting with a bag of tricks, when I suddenly found myself
surrounded by monsters.  I was (foolishly, in hindsight) standing on
the altar itself and couldn't engrave, but fortunately, I'd happened
to learn the charm monster spell, and it tamed every one of the
beasties.  But later, when I lugged a corpse back to the altar, I
found some random monster's corpse already on it.  Do I want to
sacrifice it?  Why not?  Alas, it turned out to have been one of the
friends I'd made earlier, slain by another dungeon denizen, and the
altar's god smote me.

Do these kinds of things just not happen to the real Nethack experts,
or can I expect to keep suffering annoying deaths for as long as I
play the game?


